<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Atiba Atobatele</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1859</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Atiba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Atiba Atobatele was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaafin">Alaafin</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo</a> from about 1837 to 1859. After the abandonment of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-ile">Oyo-Ile</a> he established the capital of a reduced kingdom at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-oyo">New Oyo</a>, the present city of Oyo, farther south. He tried to rebuild the realm by recognising the war leaders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibadan">Ibadan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ijaye">Ijaye</a> as its chief military officers, to defend <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yorubaland">Yorubaland</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilorin">Ilorin</a>.</p></div>
